"""Build a local review and manual tracing page. No network or new training."""
from pathlib import Path
import argparse,json,shutil
HTML=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Six root periderm measurements</title>
<style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{font:17px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Arial,sans-serif;color:#192331;background:#f7f8fa;margin:0}main{max-width:1250px;margin:30px auto;padding:0 28px 60px}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:32px}p{max-width:1000px}.panel{background:white;padding:20px;border:1px solid #ccd1d8;border-radius:9px;margin-top:18px}.muted{color:#536071;font-size:15px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white}th,td{padding:10px 13px;border:1px solid #cbd3dc;text-align:right}th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}th{background:#edf0f4}button,select,input{font:inherit;padding:8px;border:1px solid #9ca9b9;border-radius:5px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer}button:hover{background:#edf4fa}label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-right:15px;margin-bottom:9px}.toolbar{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:12px 0}.view{overflow:auto;max-height:600px;border:1px solid #8796a8;background:#020704}.view canvas{display:block;cursor:crosshair}#overview{width:100%;display:block}a{color:#154f91}.value{font-size:21px;font-weight:650}details{margin-top:22px}#message{min-height:1.5em;color:#344559}input[type=number]{width:155px}.step{font-weight:600}#length{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.warning{color:#923800}input[type=range]{padding:0;width:150px}</style>
<main><h1>Measure periderm on six roots</h1><p>We can now measure a curved path on each root. The cyan lines below use <strong>your saved Periderm outlines</strong>. The model-only estimates are kept separately because some transition positions are still wrong. This is a development proof of concept, with biological review pending.</p>
<img id="overview" src="OPEN_ME_SIX_ROOT_LENGTHS.png" alt="Six numbered roots with annotation-assisted periderm measurement paths">
<h2>Compare the lengths</h2><p>Lengths are in <strong>original image pixels</strong>. No independent manual lengths have been entered. The microscope scale for this MT25 slide is still unconfirmed.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Root</th><th>From your outlines<br>(pixels)</th><th>Model only<br>(pixels)</th><th>Your manual trace<br>(pixels)</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table>
<p><a href="SIX_ROOTS_compare_with_manual.csv" download>Download the initial comparison table</a> · <a href="../../05_Notes/06_Periderm_Length_Proof_Walkthrough.docx">Open the Word walkthrough</a></p>
<h2>Review one root or measure it yourself</h2><p><span class="step">1.</span> Choose a root. <span class="step">2.</span> Zoom in to inspect the cells. <span class="step">3.</span> For a manual measurement, click the transition, then follow the centre of the main root with several clicks to the basal end. Leave lateral roots out. Each click adds a point; the last click is the end. Use Undo if needed.</p>
<div class="panel"><div class="toolbar"><label>Root <select id="root"></select></label><label>Zoom <input type="range" id="zoom" min="1" max="12" step=".5" value="1"><span id="zoomLabel">1×</span></label><label><input type="checkbox" id="assisted">Show outline-based line</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="auto">Show model-only line</label></div>
<p class="muted">Both reference lines start hidden so you can inspect the image first. Cyan = outline-based path; orange = model-only path; magenta = your manual trace. The display can be resized; measurements always use original pixels.</p>
<div class="view" id="viewport"><canvas id="canvas" width="1000" height="200"></canvas></div>
<div class="toolbar"><button id="undo">Undo last point</button><button id="clear">Clear this manual trace</button><button id="save">Download comparison CSV</button><button id="saveJson">Download trace JSON</button></div>
<p id="length" class="value">Manual trace: no points yet</p><p id="message" aria-live="polite"></p>
<label>Confirmed pixels per micrometre <input type="number" id="calibration" step="any" min="0" placeholder="Unconfirmed"></label><p class="muted">Leave blank until this slide's scale is confirmed. The 0.5299 pixels/µm scale was confirmed for 20_29 and 2_12, not separately for MT25. Physical length = pixels ÷ pixels per µm. Fiji is not required for this calculation.</p>
<p class="warning">Manual points remain in this browser page until you close or reload it. Download before leaving. A manual trace is a measurement you provide; it does not train or change the model.</p></div>
<details><summary>What was measured and what remains to check</summary><p>Slide: MT25_rep3. Six Periderm polygons from MT25_rep3_root5_refined_GV.json, including your refined roots 4 and 5. Other roots retain your earlier practice outlines. Polygon centreline geometry is computed at quarter resolution, smoothed and converted back to original coordinates before adding Euclidean segment lengths. The comparison model is the preserved three-category PAT transfer model. Its image-only result uses a separate basal-connected periderm rule and does not read annotations.</p><p>The outline start and end may still need biological correction. Accurate path calculation cannot guarantee accurate tissue identification. This previously used slide does not establish performance on new experiments. No new model was trained for this measurement proof. More detailed raw predictions and exploratory results remain in folder 49.</p><p><a href="proof_record.json">Measurement record and provenance</a> · <a href="annotations_snapshot.json">Saved annotation snapshot</a> · <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10981931/">PAT paper</a></p></details></main>
<script>const DATA=__DATA__;
const el=id=>document.getElementById(id), roots=DATA.roots, traces=roots.map(()=>[]);let current=0,img=new Image(),drawScale=1,loaded=false;
const pixelLength=pts=>pts.slice(1).reduce((sum,p,i)=>sum+Math.hypot(p[0]-pts[i][0],p[1]-pts[i][1]),0);
const calibration=()=>{let s=el('calibration').value.trim();let n=Number(s);return s&&Number.isFinite(n)&&n>0?n:null};
function table(){el('rows').innerHTML=roots.map((r,i)=>`<tr><td>Root ${r.root_id}</td><td>${Math.round(r.annotation_assisted_length_px).toLocaleString()}</td><td>${r.automatic_length_px==null?'Unavailable':Math.round(r.automatic_length_px).toLocaleString()}</td><td>${traces[i].length<2?'Not entered':pixelLength(traces[i]).toFixed(1)}</td></tr>`).join('')}
function draw(){if(!loaded)return;const r=roots[current],box=r.review_image_box,c=el('canvas'),ctx=c.getContext('2d'),base=Math.min(1,(el('viewport').clientWidth-2)/img.naturalWidth);drawScale=base*Number(el('zoom').value);c.width=Math.round(img.naturalWidth*drawScale);c.height=Math.round(img.naturalHeight*drawScale);ctx.drawImage(img,0,0,c.width,c.height);
 const path=(pts,color,width=3)=>{if(!pts.length)return;ctx.strokeStyle=color;ctx.lineWidth=width;ctx.beginPath();pts.forEach((p,i)=>{const x=(p[0]-box[0])*drawScale,y=(p[1]-box[1])*drawScale;if(i)ctx.lineTo(x,y);else ctx.moveTo(x,y)});ctx.stroke();[pts[0],pts[pts.length-1]].forEach(p=>{ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc((p[0]-box[0])*drawScale,(p[1]-box[1])*drawScale,5,0,2*Math.PI);ctx.fillStyle=color;ctx.fill()})};
 if(el('assisted').checked)path(r.path_xy,'#00e3f0');if(el('auto').checked&&r.automatic_start_index!=null)path(r.automatic_path_xy.slice(r.automatic_start_index),'#ff9f32');path(traces[current],'#ff53e0');
 const n=traces[current].length,len=pixelLength(traces[current]),cal=calibration();el('length').textContent=n<2?`Manual trace: ${n} point${n===1?'':'s'} — add at least two`:`Manual trace: ${len.toFixed(1)} pixels${cal?` = ${(len/cal).toFixed(1)} µm`:''} (${n} points)`;el('zoomLabel').textContent=el('zoom').value+'×';table()}
function select(){current=Number(el('root').value);loaded=false;img=new Image();img.onload=()=>{loaded=true;draw()};img.src=roots[current].review_image;el('message').textContent='';}
roots.forEach((r,i)=>{const op=document.createElement('option');op.value=i;op.textContent='Root '+r.root_id;el('root').appendChild(op)});el('root').onchange=select;['zoom','assisted','auto','calibration'].forEach(id=>el(id).oninput=draw);
el('canvas').onclick=e=>{if(!loaded)return;const rect=e.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect(),box=roots[current].review_image_box;traces[current].push([box[0]+(e.clientX-rect.left)/drawScale,box[1]+(e.clientY-rect.top)/drawScale]);draw();el('message').textContent='Point added. Keep clicking along the main root, or undo.'};
el('undo').onclick=()=>{traces[current].pop();draw()};el('clear').onclick=()=>{traces[current]=[];draw();el('message').textContent='Manual trace cleared; saved model and annotations unchanged.'};
function download(name,text,type){const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([text],{type}));a.download=name;a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href),1000)}
function exportRecords(){const cal=calibration();return roots.map((r,i)=>{const len=traces[i].length>=2?pixelLength(traces[i]):null;return{root_id:r.root_id,annotation_assisted_px:r.annotation_assisted_length_px,model_only_px:r.automatic_length_px,manual_trace_px:len,manual_trace_um:len!==null&&cal?len/cal:null,pixels_per_um:cal,manual_minus_assisted_px:len===null?null:len-r.annotation_assisted_length_px,manual_minus_model_px:len===null||r.automatic_length_px==null?null:len-r.automatic_length_px,manual_points_xy:traces[i],review_status:len===null?'manual not supplied':'manual trace supplied; anatomy chosen by reviewer'}})}
el('save').onclick=()=>{let records=exportRecords(),keys=Object.keys(records[0]).filter(k=>k!=='manual_points_xy'),quote=v=>v==null?'':`"${String(v).replaceAll('"','""')}"`,csv=keys.join(',')+'\n'+records.map(r=>keys.map(k=>quote(r[k])).join(',')).join('\n')+'\n';download('MT25_six_root_manual_comparison.csv',csv,'text/csv');el('message').textContent='CSV download requested. Also download the trace JSON to keep your points.'};
el('saveJson').onclick=()=>{download('MT25_six_root_manual_traces.json',JSON.stringify({exported_at:new Date().toISOString(),source_image:DATA.source_image,source_sha256:DATA.source_sha256,annotation_sha256:DATA.annotations_sha256,measurements:exportRecords()},null,2),'application/json');el('message').textContent='Trace JSON download requested. Check your Downloads folder.'};
window.proofReview={pixelLength,exportRecords,traces,get current(){return current}};window.addEventListener('resize',draw);table();select();</script></html>'''
def main(folder):
 data=json.loads((folder/'proof_record.json').read_text());(folder/'OPEN_ME_REVIEW_AND_MEASURE.html').write_text(HTML.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('</','<\\/')));shutil.copy2(__file__,folder/Path(__file__).name)
if __name__=='__main__':
 p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('folder',type=Path);main(p.parse_args().folder)
